#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124629 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124433 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/id #uuid "c1120305-c8cb-5f57-97b1-9b31dc059b4a" :question/math-academy-id "e-9961" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n*If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\text{__________}\\,.$*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\nI. $\\det(A) = 0$\n\nII. $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n$\n\nIII. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns" :question/worked-solution "The invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$A$ is invertible ![](images/dc/dc72aea1969143a926fd637d3360bb42116b27545a748923069f4ae732bd700f.svg)\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the options separately.\n\n- The following statement is false:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\det(A) = 0.$* $\\:{\\color{red}\\times}$\n\nSince $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ must be invertible, which means $\\det(A) \\ne 0.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $\\textrm{rank}(A) = n.$* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$\n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{rank}(A)=n.$\n\n- The following statement is true:\n\n$\\qquad$ *If $A$ is a $n\\times n$ matrix and $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\{\\mathbf{ 0}\\},$ then $A$ has $n$ pivot columns.* $\\:{\\color{green}\\checkmark}$ \n\nIndeed, since $A$ is invertible, then according to the invertible matrix theorem, we have $\\textrm{dim(Col}(A))=n,$ which means that $A$ has exactly $n$ pivot columns.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125167 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bec134f4-8ac1-5fd3-a994-79031801df9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123603} {:answer/id #uuid "e52ece27-d671-527d-aac5-dac055efd06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123604} {:answer/id #uuid "2e01b189-5d9a-582b-a3da-d616b84586a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123605} {:answer/id #uuid "32960b14-b04a-59a2-9224-0b8a82626700" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffd9fe3-d1f5-5a30-b5aa-c6b01c0e6506" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123607}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9eda024b-b844-536e-bf1a-f1efd2375bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123602}] :question/id #uuid "f935b331-7ef7-5abb-b2c6-c78c4160f9a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-47586" :question/problem "Consider the following sentence:\n\n> *If $A$ is a $n \\cdot n$ matrix and $det(A) \\ne 0$, then $__________$.*\n\nWhich of the following can be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?\n\n1. $A$ has no inverse\n2. $Null(A)$ has no basis\n3. $A$ has $n$ pivot columns"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bb90e5b9-03fe-51cf-bc16-a293befacebc" :knowledge-point/title "Сompleting a Sentence Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem"}